# Design system

Target: luxury Swiss watch × futuristic command center × elite performance
laboratory × personal AI intelligence. "2075 sophistication", not decoration.
Full reference: `docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`.

## Palette and tokens

- Base is true obsidian black. Gold is authority/primary action. Purple is
  intelligence state (Atlas thinking, streaming, memory activity). Purple is
  an accent, never a wash. No neon, no cheap gradients.
- All tokens are Tailwind 4 `@theme` variables in
  `src/design/tokens/theme.css` (OKLCH). Components consume tokens; never
  hardcode colors, radii, shadows, or durations.
- Surfaces are layered by elevation tokens (`--surface-0..4`) with restrained
  translucency. Avoid stacks of rounded cards; use spatial layering, hairline
  dividers, and typographic hierarchy.
- Radii are small (`--radius-xs..md`); large pills only for controls that are
  literally toggles or chips.

## Typography

One display face for headings/numerals, one text face for body, one mono for
data. Numerals use tabular figures. Typography carries hierarchy before color
does.

## Motion

- Motion communicates system state (Atlas listening, thinking, streaming,
  committing to memory, environment transitions). If an animation does not
  encode state or spatial relationship, remove it.
- Use `motion/react` for component motion and React 19.3 `<ViewTransition>`
  for route/environment transitions. Durations and easings come from tokens.
- Animate `transform` and `opacity` only. Never animate layout properties in
  loops. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` in every animation.

## Responsive environment modes

Three intentional modes, exposed via `useEnvironmentMode()` and CSS:

- `compact`  — Galaxy Fold closed / phones: command bar, brief, conversation.
- `portable` — Fold open / tablets: two-pane command center.
- `command`  — desktop: full operating environment.

Detection order: `device-posture` + viewport segments (Chromium) → container
queries → width fallback. Layout must never span the hinge: use
`env(viewport-segment-*)` when `horizontal-viewport-segments: 2`. Every
screen must be tested in all three modes.

## Accessibility and performance

- Keyboard reachable, visible focus (gold ring), semantic landmarks, ARIA
  only where semantics are missing. Use Base UI/Radix primitives for dialogs,
  menus, and popovers rather than hand-rolling focus management.
- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 for text on obsidian. Verify gold and purple text tokens.
- No WebGL/3D in Phase 1. Cinematic depth comes from layering, lighting
  gradients on surfaces, and motion.
- Budget: LCP < 2.5s on mid-range Android over 4G, no long tasks > 50ms
  during streaming.
